<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!-- Base application theme. -->
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="Theme.AppCompat.Light.DarkActionBar">
        <!-- Customize your theme here. -->
        <item name="colorPrimary">@color/colorPrimary</item>
        <item name="colorPrimaryDark">@color/colorPrimaryDark</item>
        <item name="colorAccent">@color/colorAccent</item>
    </style>

    <style name="AppTheme.NoActionBar" parent="Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.NoActionBar">
        <item name="windowActionBar">false</item>
        <item name="windowNoTitle">true</item>
        <item name="android:background">@null</item>
    </style>


    <!--
      Launch theme. Read this before changing anything here — what actually
      paints the launch screen is not obvious from the Capacitor template.

      `Theme.SplashScreen` (androidx core-splashscreen) is what decides it, and
      it resolves differently per API level:

        API 24-30  the library's values/ theme sets android:windowBackground to
                   @drawable/compat_splash_screen_no_icon_background, a
                   layer-list of ?windowSplashScreenBackground plus
                   ?windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon drawn in a 288dp box and
                   masked to a 192dp circle.
        API 31+    the library's values-v31/ theme maps those same two attrs
                   onto android:windowSplashScreenBackground and
                   android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon, i.e. the platform's
                   system splash screen, which targetSdk 31+ cannot opt out of.

      So both paths read the same two attributes, and setting them here covers
      every supported API level. A values-v31/ copy is not needed and would
      only be a second place to drift.

      Leaving them unset is what shipped up to v1.5.14, and it fails silently:
      below API 31 the library falls back to @android:drawable/sym_def_app_icon
      on ?android:colorBackground, and from 31 up the attrs resolve to nothing
      so the platform substitutes the launcher icon on its own default ground.
      Nothing errors; the cold start simply is not ours.
    -->
    <style name="AppTheme.NoActionBarLaunch" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <!--
          Kept from the Capacitor template, and deliberately not removed, but
          be aware that nothing appears to read it: `android:background` is a
          View attribute, whereas the window is painted from
          `android:windowBackground`, which Theme.SplashScreen.Common already
          claims above. @drawable/splash and its 10 density variants are still
          in the tree; treat them as unverified rather than load-bearing.
        -->
        <item name="android:background">@drawable/splash</item>

        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/splash_background</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_icon</item>

        <!--
          The contract androidx documents for Theme.SplashScreen. It is inert
          today: the only reader is SplashScreen.installSplashScreen(), and
          nothing calls it — Capacitor's BridgeActivity.onCreate() does the
          swap itself with setTheme(R.style.AppTheme_NoActionBar). Kept so the
          theme is still correct if @capacitor/splash-screen is ever added.
        -->
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/AppTheme.NoActionBar</item>
    </style>
</resources>